@startuml
title M-SH1 - Logical host concerns and account boundaries (SH2+ target)
left to right direction

component "Optional board client\nor authorised launching caller\ninitiating account" as caller
database "Optional goal ledger / board evidence\nowner: board; not host lifecycle" as board_state
component "agent-session-bridge\nprocess UID unspecified in spec §3.7" as bridge
database "Mailbox\nowner: bridge" as mailbox
component "swarma-dispatcher\nadmission / execution / cleanup process" as dispatcher
database "Execution / allocation / admission records\nowner: dispatcher" as execution
component "swarma-user-manager / swarma-user-launcher\nprivileged generation / stop / root launch boundary" as manager
database "Active-generation ledger\nowner: user manager (root-owned)" as generations
component "swarma-credential-broker\nauth-owner process" as broker

package "swarma-session-host process / service account\nlogical responsibilities, not a published code decomposition" {
  component "Session engine / controller" as engine
  component "Peer identity / capability admission\nfence / epoch / op_id checks" as admission
  component "Durable transcript / receipt handling" as receipts
  component "Optional goal revision application" as goals
  component "Inbox / wake / liveness" as wake
  component "Pending native interaction / approval" as approval
  component "Provider readiness / acknowledgement adapters" as adapters
  database "Host-private durable metadata, logs, transcripts, receipts\nfences / epochs / inbox / goal revisions\nowner: host service" as durable
}
component "swarma-session-runner\nworker-<label>; one per session\nPTY master / private app-server transport / lease client" as runner
component "Claude Code / Codex private app-server\nworker-<label>; provider harness process" as harness

caller --> board_state : optional board transactions
caller --> admission : generic optional goal / session calls
bridge --> mailbox : durable mail ownership
bridge --> admission : enqueue; durable host write before acknowledgement
admission --> generations : verify active managed generation
admission --> engine : admit effects only with valid fence / epoch / authority
engine --> dispatcher : execution start / stop / absence and cleanup
dispatcher --> execution : owns execution records
dispatcher --> manager : stop via exec.stop
manager --> generations : owns generation records
engine --> receipts : reconcile unknown before reopening
engine --> goals : optional revision handling
engine --> wake : turn boundary / wedge recovery
engine --> approval : pending interaction resolution
goals --> durable : record revision
wake --> durable : durable inbox / fence state
approval --> durable : durable receipt / interaction state
receipts --> durable : authoritative audit / transcript / receipts
engine --> adapters : current runner input and readiness
adapters <--> runner : host-authorised input / harness ack / heartbeat
runner --> harness : transport owner
runner --> broker : renew execution credential lease

note bottom of admission
  Refusal: wrong peer, inactive/unknown generation, invalid capability,
  stale epoch, unsupported starter; agent account has no goal capability.
  Unknown permits remain owned; unreadable state is closed.
  Machine-local context policy stays independent of board facts (§2.3).
end note
note bottom of receipts
  Matching input marker in intact transcript proves applied.
  Confirmed absence permits redelivery; unresolved stays unknown.
  Unknown approval/control effect cannot auto-replay (§3.4).
end note
note bottom of engine
  Recovery: no runner input before reconciliation; live authenticated runner
  re-adoption retains execution ID, new exec gets new ID (§3.2).
  Explicit stop stays stopped; park is durable; restart owns its fence (§3.5).
  Internal APIs / engine classes: unspecified in spec §3.
end note
note bottom of adapters
  Unknown readiness parks; Muse requires qualification.
  Codex renewal timeout fails turn with no fallback (§3.2).
  Current / SH1: all serving concerns remain composed into tb-sessiond;
  daemon owns Claude PTY and private Codex app-server (§1, §2).
  Claude: exact rendered revision ack / deferral; Codex: text directives,
  native goals disabled. Muse adapter behavior retained but unregistered.
  Muse factories stay unregistered; hosted capability route refuses.
end note
note bottom of approval
  First valid CAS resolution only; ordinary user turn is not approval.
  Restart invalidates historical approval; fence invalidates pending interaction.
  Receipt / approval and optional goal wire/state schemas:
  unspecified in spec §7; publication is an activation gate.
end note

